   "verdict": "WRONG IN BOTH DIRECTIONS, and the two errors have different causes. Against the shipping call (0.463 s) it under-predicts by 2.3x, because it models the ray x pixel reconstruction and the call is dominated by the O(N^2) ray-density diagnostic. Against the reconstruction alone (0.055 s) it over-predicts by 3.7x, because its _RAY_PIXEL_PRODUCTS_PER_SECOND constant is not calibrated to this host. A planner ordering work by this number would be wrong about which node is expensive, which is the failure that matters."
